,"children":"The UUID (Universally Unique Identifier) Generator is a free developer utility that instantly creates highly unique, RFC 4122 compliant identifiers. Also known as GUIDs (Globally Unique Identifiers) in the Microsoft ecosystem, these 128-bit identifiers are essential for database primary keys, session IDs, and distributed systems."}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold mb-3 mt-8 text-white","children":"Supported UUID Versions"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"list-disc pl-5 mb-6 text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] space-y-2","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Version 4 (Random):"}]," The most common type of UUID. It relies on random numbers, ensuring an extremely low probability of collision (duplication). Ideal for almost all general-purpose identifier needs."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Version 1 (Time-based):"}]," Generated using the current timestamp and the computer's MAC address (or a random node ID). Useful when you need identifiers that can be sorted by creation time."]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold mb-3 mt-8 text-white","children":"Features"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"list-disc pl-5 mb-6 text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] space-y-2","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Bulk Generation:"}]," Generate up to 100 UUIDs at once with a single click."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Zero Server Communication:"}]," UUIDs are generated directly in your browser using secure cryptographic APIs (`crypto.randomUUID()`), meaning they are generated instantly and securely without network requests."]}]]}]]}]],[["$","script","script-0",{"src":"/_next/static/chunks/470e47fc3d8ef718.js","async":true}]],"$L4"]}],"loading":null,"isPartial":false}
